# Publish the Hylé CLI to a private registry (e.g. JFrog Artifactory) instead of npmjs.
# Copy to .npmrc and fill in. For a scoped package, scope the registry line.
#
# Official npmjs (default — no .npmrc needed):
#   npm publish
#
# Artifactory / private registry:
registry=https://your-company.jfrog.io/artifactory/api/npm/npm-local/
# Auth token (prefer an env var in CI, not a committed file):
//your-company.jfrog.io/artifactory/api/npm/npm-local/:_authToken=${NPM_TOKEN}
#
# Install from the private registry on a developer machine:
#   npm config set registry https://your-company.jfrog.io/artifactory/api/npm/npm-local/
#   npm install -g hyle
